# CANONICAL §7.3 fixture — `Hole.points` (ONECAD-361, `resultPolicyVersion: 3`).
#
# WHAT IS PINNED HERE. No measured geometry number appears (`signatures.geometry`
# is `$hex64`); the analytic volumes, per-point through-all, the slot-narrowed
# ladder and FeaturePattern live in worker/tests/test_hole_points.cpp, which can
# measure a solid. This file pins the protocol shape a Rust or UI reader branches
# on:
#   ROUND 1  — a 3-point V3 Hole yields the SAME planStep payload shape a single
#              hole does: one `modified` event, nothing minted. DISCARDED.
#   ROUND 2  — `points[1]` outside the face refuses the WHOLE feature with
#              reasonCode HOLE_POINT_OUTSIDE_FACE + evidence.pointIndex 1.
#   ROUND 3  — coincident points: HOLE_POINTS_COINCIDENT (pointIndex/otherPointIndex).
#   ROUND 4  — `points` beside resultPolicyVersion 2: HOLE_POINTS_REQUIRE_V3.
#   ROUND 5  — `point` != `points[0].at`: HOLE_POINT_MISMATCH.
#   ROUND 6  — ROUND 1 again, ACCEPTED.
#   ROUND 7  — AcquireElementIds on hole `hp_c`'s top rim returns its producer
#              slot in `descriptor.originSlot` — the evidence Rust freezes into
#              the ref intent so a later point edit can never bind a sibling.
# Every refusal is top-level OP_FAILED at stage `preflight`; the head after the
# refusal rounds is the head before them, field for field.
#
# The Rust lane for this file is parse-only (onecad-protocol messages.rs); the
# executable cross-track coverage is this CTest plus the real-worker
# crates/onecad-app/tests/hole_points.rs.
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"hello","seq":0}}
